Third-party components
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Vera runs entirely on-device and does not bundle these; it calls or optionally
integrates with them at runtime. They remain the property of their authors under
their own licenses, and are credited here.

Local model runtimes (called at runtime, not distributed with Vera):
  • Ollama — local LLM server. https://ollama.com  (MIT License)
  • LM Studio / any OpenAI-compatible local server — optional backend.
  • Apple Intelligence / Foundation Models — optional on-device backend (Apple).

Local models the user may pull and run (not distributed with Vera):
  • Qwen2.5 (Alibaba) — used via Ollama, under its own model license.
  • Llama 3.x (Meta) — used via Ollama, under the Llama Community License.
  • nomic-embed-text (Nomic AI) — embeddings for on-device RAG, under its license.
  • Whisper (OpenAI) — optional speech-to-text, MIT License.

Voice:
  • Coqui XTTS — on-device voice synthesis, used for the optional cloned voice,
    under the Coqui Public Model License / its stated terms. The user's own voice
    recording never leaves the device.

Inspiration / acknowledgement:
  • OpenJarvis ("Personal AI, on personal devices") — spirit and idea only;
    Vera is an original, independent implementation (Ankur Sinha's own code),
    not a fork or copy of OpenJarvis.

Companion tools by the same author:
  • Voice Harvester (Ankur Sinha) — extracts a clean voice sample for cloning.
  • Unhosted (unhosted-ai) — optional pooled local inference backend.

